    "assistantText": "Location confirmed: DSH discovers project skills at `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (dsh-skill-filesystem), with `.agents/skills/` as the alternate root.\nThe skill is written and registered. The session skill catalog picked it up on its own, which confirms DSH discovered it at `.dsh/skills/`.\n\nWhat I created under [.dsh/skills/pre-commit-check](.dsh/skills/pre-commit-check):\n\n- [SKILL.md](.dsh/skills/pre-commit-check/SKILL.md) — five steps: fix the scope, run the mechanical checks, read the diff, report and fix, state the verdict. Frontmatter has `name` and `description` with the trigger branches spelled out.\n- [scripts/checks.sh](.dsh/skills/pre-commit-check/scripts/checks.sh) — the mechanical half. It prints debug leftovers, work markers, possible secrets, conflict markers, trailing whitespace, and generated or oversized files. It never exits non-zero, so every finding still needs a judgement.\n- [references/checklist.md](.dsh/skills/pre-commit-check/references/checklist.md) — the rule list behind the judgement calls, split into blocking, non-blocking, and judgement rules, disclosed behind a pointer so the main file stays a recipe.\n\nTwo design decisions worth naming:\n\nThe location is `.dsh/skills/`, not `.cursor/skills/`. The pstack harness adapter maps Cursor's path to DSH's, and the `dsh-skill-filesystem` package scans `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills` (with `.agents/skills` as the alternate root). The catalog update listing `pre-commit-check` is the proof that the path is right.\n\nThe script stays a script. Hand-running six greps over a change set every time is the kind of repeated work that belongs in a tool a reviewer can rerun, so the mechanical half is one command and the diff reading stays with the agent.\n\nI ran the script in this repo as a smoke test. It reported the empty scope and listed the four untracked files, including itself. That is the expected result here, since nothing is staged.",
